       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. CGENHELP.
       AUTHOR.     MARVIN MITCHELL.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. AS400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. AS400.
       SPECIAL-NAMES. I-O-FEEDBACK IS I-O-FEEDBACK-AREA.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.

      *D  ONCE CALLED:
      *D        CGENHELP will switch from the current screen of the
      *D    calling program to the FGENHELP help screen located in
      *D    the ZGENHELP display file.
      *D
      *D        It will then search the MVALIDTYPE (MCFPCS5100) data-
      *D    database for the TYPE-CODE passed via the CGENHELP-TYPE
      *D    field.  If the type-code is found, it will retrieve all
      *D    records in the DVALIDDATA (MCFPCS5200) database that are
      *D    linked to that type code.
      *D
      *D        The program then displays those records on the help
      *D    screen and lets the user choose the code of their choice
      *D    by placing an X to the left of that code and description
      *D    and pressing <ENTER>.
      *D
      *D  ****  IF A CODE IS SELECTED:
      *D           The program returns to the calling program with
      *D           selected code in the CGENHELP-CODE field.
      *D
      *D  ****  IF NO CODE IS SELECTED:
      *D           The program moves spaces to the CGENHELP-CODE
      *D           field and returns to the calling program.
      *D
      *D  ****  IF AN ERROR IS DETECTED:
      *D           The program will move a message to the field
      *D           BU-DISPLAY-MSG and debugging info to the
      *D           BU-DISPLAY-AREA fields 4 and 5.
      *D        OTHERWISE:
      *D           BU-DISPLAY-MSG  will contain spaces and
      *D           BU-DISPLAY-AREA will contain zeros.
      *D
      *D    BEFORE RETURNING TO THE CALLING PROGRAM:
      *D        CGENHELP will redisplay the screen that was on the
      *D        CRT before it was called.
      *D
      *D    The following FOUR parameters are required to execute
      *D    this program on the AS/400:
      *D
      *D    PARAMETERS:
      *D       BU-DISPLAY-AREA         Returns:
      *D                                 ZEROS if no errors occur.
      *D
      *D                                 DEBUGGING INFORMATION in
      *D                                 BU-DISPLAY-FLDS 4 and 5 if
      *D                                 an ERROR is detected.
      *D
      *D       BU-DISPLAY-MSG          Returns:
      *D                                 SPACES of no errors occur.
      *D
      *D                                 Message to help locate the
      *D                                 problem if an error occurs.
      *D
      *D       CGENHELP-PARMS
      *D         01  CGENHELP-PARMS.
      *D             05  CGENHELP-KEY.
      *D                 10  CGENHELP-TYPE    PIC X(6).
      *D                 10  CGENHELP-TYPE    PIC X(6).
      *D
      *D         Passed:
      *D           Type Code in the CGENHELP-TYPE field.
      *D
      *D         Returns:
      *D           SPACES in CGENHELP-CODE in no selection
      *D           is made.
      *D
      *D           Valid Code in CGENHELP-CODE if a selection
      *D           is made.
      *D
      *D       VIEW-COMARE             Passed:
      *D                                 Name of current screen.
      *D
      *D    ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:
      *D       1)  The CGENHELP-PARMS field CGENHELP-TYPE must contain
      *D           a valid six character type code.

       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT DISPLAY-FILE
               ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-ZGENHELP-SI
               ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
               FILE STATUS IS DSPLY-STATUS
               CONTROL-AREA IS WS-CONTROL.

           SELECT MVALID-FILE
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS5101
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                   WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DVALID-FILE
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS5201
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  DISPLAY-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
       01  DSPLY-REC                   PIC X(2000).

       FD  MVALID-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  TYPE-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCS5101.

       FD  DVALID-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DATA-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCS5201.

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

       COPY CATREAD  OF COPYLIB.
       COPY DVLDDATA IN COPYLIB.
       COPY CPYIND OF COPYLIB.
       COPY IOFEEDBACK OF COPYLIB.
       COPY MVLDTYPE IN COPYLIB.
       COPY WSCONTROL OF COPYLIB.

       01  COUNTERS.
           05  CURRENT-SCREEN-NO         PIC 99 COMP-3 VALUE 0.
           05  ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN         PIC 99 COMP-3 VALUE 0.
           05  SCREEN-INDEX              PIC 99 COMP-3 VALUE 1.

       01  DSPLY-STATUS.
           05  DSPLY-STATUS-1            PIC X     VALUE "0".
           05  DSPLY-STATUS-2            PIC X     VALUE "0".

       COPY DBSTAT IN COPYLIB.

       01  FILE-STATUS.
           05  FILE-STATUS-1             PIC X     VALUE "0".
           05  FILE-STATUS-2             PIC X     VALUE "0".

       01  FHELPSC1.
           COPY DD-FHELPSC1 OF ZGENHELP.

       01  SAVE-KEY.
           05  SAVE-TYPE                 PIC X(6)  VALUE SPACES.
           05  SAVE-CODE                 PIC X(6)  VALUE SPACES.

       01  SWITCHES.
           05  EOF-SW                    PIC X     VALUE "N".
           05  TOF-SW                    PIC X     VALUE "N".
           05  FULL-SCREEN-SW            PIC X     VALUE "N".
           05  TOP-OF-CURRENT-SCREEN-SW  PIC X     VALUE "N".

       01  CGENHELP-VIEW-CFNAME          PIC X(16).

       01  WS-DISPLAY-AREA.
           05    FILLER                  PIC XX.
           05  WS-DISPLAY-MSG            PIC X(27).
           05    FILLER                  PIC XX.
           05  WS-DISPLAY-STAT           PIC S9(4).
           05    FILLER                  PIC XX.
           05  WS-DISPLAY-FLD            PIC X(14).
           05    FILLER                  PIC XX.

       01  WS-SCREEN.
           05  MVALID-DESC-WS            PIC X(50).
           05  WS-DETAIL.
               10  WS-ENTRIES   OCCURS  28  TIMES.
                   15  WS-X              PIC X.
                   15  WS-CODE           PIC X(6).
                   15  WS-DESC           PIC X(30).

      ***************************************
      *     L I N K A G E  S E C T I O N    *
      ***************************************
       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01  BU-DISPLAY-AREA               PIC X(110).
       01  BU-DISPLAY-FLDS REDEFINES BU-DISPLAY-AREA.
           05  BU-DISPLAY-LINE OCCURS 5 TIMES.
               10  BU-DISPLAY-FLD        PIC X(14).
               10  BU-DISPLAY-FLD9       PIC S9(8).

       01  BU-DISPLAY-MSG.
           05  BU-DISPLAY-MSG-1          PIC X.
           05  BU-DISPLAY-MSG-2          PIC X(57).
           05  BU-DISPLAY-PARA           PIC X(2).

       COPY CGENHELP    OF COPYLIB.

       COPY VCOMLINK    OF COPYLIB.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION  USING
                                 BU-DISPLAY-AREA,
                                 BU-DISPLAY-MSG,
                                 CGENHELP-PARMS,
                                 VIEW-COMAREA.

       START-PROGRAM.
           PERFORM 1-HOUSEKEEPING THRU 1-EXIT.
           PERFORM 6-MAIN         THRU 6-EXIT
           PERFORM 2-END-OF-JOB   THRU 2-EXIT.
           GOBACK.

       1-HOUSEKEEPING.
           MOVE SPACES TO BUF-DVALIDDATA.
           MOVE SPACES TO BUF-MVALIDTYPE.
           MOVE 0      TO CURRENT-SCREEN-NO.
           MOVE 0      TO ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN.
           MOVE 1      TO SCREEN-INDEX.
           MOVE ZEROS  TO DSPLY-STATUS.
           MOVE "0"    TO DSPLY-STATUS-2.
           MOVE ZEROS  TO STATUS-AREA.
           MOVE ZEROS  TO FILE-STATUS.
           MOVE SPACES TO FHELPSC1.
           MOVE SPACES TO SAVE-KEY.
           MOVE "N"    TO   EOF-SW,
                            TOF-SW,
                            FULL-SCREEN-SW,
                            TOP-OF-CURRENT-SCREEN-SW.
           MOVE SPACES TO  WS-DISPLAY-AREA.

           OPEN I-O DISPLAY-FILE.
           OPEN INPUT MVALID-FILE.
           OPEN INPUT DVALID-FILE.
           MOVE SPACES       TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG.

       1-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       2-END-OF-JOB.
           CLOSE MVALID-FILE.
           CLOSE DVALID-FILE.
           CLOSE DISPLAY-FILE.

       2-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       30-READ-FORWARD.
           READ DVALID-FILE NEXT
             INTO BUF-DVALIDDATA
               AT END
                 MOVE "Y" TO EOF-SW.

       30-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       31-READ-BACKWARD.
           READ DVALID-FILE PRIOR
             INTO BUF-DVALIDDATA
               AT END
                 MOVE "Y" TO TOF-SW.

       31-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       6-MAIN.
           MOVE "FHELPSC1" TO CGENHELP-VIEW-CFNAME.

           MOVE CGENHELP-TYPE TO VLDCODETYP OF DATA-REC,
                                 VLDCODETYP OF TYPE-REC,
                                 SAVE-TYPE.
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-SCREEN, CGENHELP-CODE.

           PERFORM 60-START-LIST THRU 60-EXIT.

       6-PUT-BUFFER.
           MOVE WS-SCREEN TO FHELPSC1.
           MOVE FHELPSC1 TO DSPLY-REC.

       6-SHOW.
           PERFORM 99-SCREEN-WRITE THRU 99-EXIT.

       6-READ.
           PERFORM 98-SCREEN-READ  THRU 98-EXIT.

       6-PROCESS.
           IF VIEW-LASTKEY = 3
             GO TO 6-EXIT
           ELSE
             IF VIEW-LASTKEY = 7
                 IF TOF-SW = "Y"
                     CLOSE DVALID-FILE
                     OPEN INPUT DVALID-FILE
                     READ DVALID-FILE FIRST INTO BUF-DVALIDDATA
                     MOVE "N" TO TOF-SW
                     MOVE  0  TO SCREEN-INDEX
                     PERFORM 67-NEXT-SCREEN THRU 66-EXIT
                     GO TO 6-PUT-BUFFER
                 ELSE
                 PERFORM 67-NEXT-SCREEN THRU 67-EXIT
                 GO TO 6-PUT-BUFFER
             ELSE
               IF VIEW-LASTKEY = 6
                 IF EOF-SW = "Y"
                     CLOSE DVALID-FILE
                     OPEN INPUT DVALID-FILE
                     READ DVALID-FILE LAST INTO BUF-DVALIDDATA
                     PERFORM 31-READ-BACKWARD THRU 31-EXIT
                         UNTIL (VALID-CODE-TYPE = VALID-TYPE-CODE)
                             OR (TOF-SW = "Y")
                     SUBTRACT 1 FROM ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN
                     PERFORM 66-PREVIOUS-SCREEN THRU 66-EXIT
                     GO TO 6-PUT-BUFFER
                 ELSE
                 PERFORM 66-PREVIOUS-SCREEN THRU 66-EXIT
                 GO TO 6-PUT-BUFFER.
      *****   The following section of code is not needed for operation
      *****   on the AS/400.  If the use of a function key is not
      *****   specified in SDU, the program will automatically inform
      *****   the user that the key selected is invalid.
      *****
      *****    ELSE
      *****      IF VIEW-LASTKEY > 7  OR
      *****          VIEW-LASTKEY = 5  OR
      *****           VIEW-LASTKEY = 4   OR
      *****             VIEW-LASTKEY = 3  OR
      *****               VIEW-LASTKEY = 2  OR
      *****                 VIEW-LASTKEY = 1
      *****        MOVE 09  TO LANG-SETNUM
      *****        MOVE 010 TO LANG-MSGNUM
      *****        PERFORM 999-CATREAD THRU 999-EXIT
      *****        PERFORM 6-PUT-BUFFER
      *****        GO TO 6-SHOW.

           MOVE DSPLY-REC TO WS-SCREEN.
           MOVE   1       TO SCREEN-INDEX.
           PERFORM 61-CHECK-FOR-X THRU 61-EXIT.

       6-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       60-START-LIST.
      *****  This paragraph initially fills the list screen with values.

           START MVALID-FILE
               KEY IS EQUAL TO VLDCODETYP OF TYPE-REC
                 INVALID KEY
                   MOVE "**ERROR** INVALID TYPE CODE PASSED TO CGENHELP"
                       TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
                   GO TO 99-BLOWUP.

           READ MVALID-FILE  INTO  BUF-MVALIDTYPE
             INVALID KEY
               MOVE "INVALID KEY ERROR FOR MVALID IN 60-"
                   TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
               GO TO 99-BLOWUP.

           MOVE VALID-TYPE-DESC TO MVALID-DESC-WS.

           START DVALID-FILE
               KEY IS EQUAL TO VLDCODETYP OF DATA-REC
                 INVALID KEY
                    MOVE "Y" TO EOF-SW
                    MOVE  0  TO ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN
                    MOVE  1  TO CURRENT-SCREEN-NO.

           IF EOF-SW = "N"
             PERFORM 67-NEXT-SCREEN THRU 67-EXIT.

       60-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       61-CHECK-FOR-X.
      *****  This paragraph checks to see if the user has selected a
      *****  code and description from the list screen.

           IF SCREEN-INDEX > ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN  OR
              SCREEN-INDEX > 28
             GO TO 61-EXIT.

           IF WS-X (SCREEN-INDEX) NOT = SPACES
             MOVE WS-CODE (SCREEN-INDEX) TO CGENHELP-CODE
             GO TO 61-EXIT
           ELSE
             ADD 1 TO SCREEN-INDEX
             GO TO 61-CHECK-FOR-X.

       61-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       66-PREVIOUS-SCREEN.
      *****  This paragraph checks to see which record the program
      *****  is pointing to before filling the screen buffer with
      *****  the values for the previous screen.
      *****
      *****  The TOP-OF-CURRENT-PAGE-SW is used to let the program
      *****  know whether it is pointing to the first or last record
      *****  on the current screen.  If the program is pointing to
      *****  the last record on the current screen, it must traverse
      *****  BACKWARD 28 records to account for the records that are
      *****  currently on the screen, and then traverse BACKWARDS
      *****  28 more records to fill the PREVIOUS screen.
      *****  If the program is pointing to the first record of the
      *****  current screen, it must only traverse BACKWARDS through
      *****  28 valid records to fill the PREVIOUS screen.

           IF CURRENT-SCREEN-NO = 1
             GO TO 66-EXIT
           ELSE
             IF EOF-SW = "Y"
               MOVE ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN TO SCREEN-INDEX
             ELSE
               MOVE 28 TO SCREEN-INDEX.

           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DETAIL.

           IF TOP-OF-CURRENT-SCREEN-SW = "N"
             MOVE "N" TO FULL-SCREEN-SW
             PERFORM 660-FILL-PREVIOUS THRU 660-EXIT
                 UNTIL FULL-SCREEN-SW = "Y"
             MOVE 28 TO SCREEN-INDEX
             MOVE "N" TO FULL-SCREEN-SW
             PERFORM 660-FILL-PREVIOUS THRU 660-EXIT
                 UNTIL FULL-SCREEN-SW = "Y"
             MOVE "Y" TO TOP-OF-CURRENT-SCREEN-SW
           ELSE
             MOVE "N" TO FULL-SCREEN-SW
             PERFORM 660-FILL-PREVIOUS THRU 660-EXIT
                 UNTIL FULL-SCREEN-SW = "Y".

           MOVE "N" TO EOF-SW.
           SUBTRACT 1 FROM CURRENT-SCREEN-NO.

       66-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       660-FILL-PREVIOUS.
      *****  This paragraph fills the buffer with the values for
      *****  the previous screen.

           PERFORM 31-READ-BACKWARD THRU 31-EXIT.
           IF VALID-CODE-TYPE NOT = SAVE-TYPE
             MOVE "Y" TO TOF-SW
             PERFORM 30-READ-FORWARD THRU 30-EXIT.

           IF TOF-SW = "Y"
             MOVE 0 TO SCREEN-INDEX
             GO TO 660-CHECK.

           IF VALID-CODE-DESC = SPACES
             NEXT SENTENCE
           ELSE
             MOVE SPACE            TO  WS-X (SCREEN-INDEX)
             MOVE VALID-CODE-KEY   TO  SAVE-KEY
             MOVE SAVE-CODE        TO  WS-CODE (SCREEN-INDEX)
             MOVE VALID-CODE-DESC  TO  WS-DESC (SCREEN-INDEX)
             SUBTRACT 1 FROM SCREEN-INDEX.

       660-CHECK.
           IF TOF-SW = "Y"
             MOVE "Y" TO FULL-SCREEN-SW
           ELSE
             IF SCREEN-INDEX < 1
               MOVE "Y" TO FULL-SCREEN-SW.

       660-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       67-NEXT-SCREEN.
      *****  This paragraph checks to see which record the program
      *****  is pointing to before filling the screen buffer with
      *****  values for the NEXT screen.
      *****
      *****  The TOP-OF-CURRENT-PAGE-SW is used to let the program
      *****  know whether it is pointing to the first or last record
      *****  on the current screen.  If the program is pointing to
      *****  the first record on the current screen, it must traverse
      *****  FORWARDS 28 records to account for the records that are
      *****  currently listed on the screen, and then traverse FOR-
      *****  WARD 28 more records to fill the NEXT screen.
      *****  If the program is pointing to the last record of the
      *****  current screen, it must only traverse FORWARDS through
      *****  28 valid records to fill the NEXT screen.

           IF EOF-SW = "Y"
              GO TO 67-EXIT.

           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DETAIL.
           MOVE   1    TO SCREEN-INDEX.
           MOVE  "N"   TO FULL-SCREEN-SW.

           IF TOP-OF-CURRENT-SCREEN-SW = "N"
             PERFORM 670-FILL-NEXT THRU 670-EXIT
                 UNTIL FULL-SCREEN-SW = "Y"
           ELSE
             PERFORM 670-FILL-NEXT THRU 670-EXIT
                 UNTIL FULL-SCREEN-SW = "Y"
             MOVE SPACES TO WS-DETAIL
             MOVE  "N"   TO FULL-SCREEN-SW
             MOVE   1    TO SCREEN-INDEX
             PERFORM 670-FILL-NEXT THRU 670-EXIT
                 UNTIL FULL-SCREEN-SW = "Y".

           MOVE "N"  TO TOP-OF-CURRENT-SCREEN-SW.
           ADD   1   TO CURRENT-SCREEN-NO.

       67-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       670-FILL-NEXT.
      *****  This paragraph fills the buffer with the values for the
      *****  next list screen.

           IF VALID-CODE-DESC = SPACES
             GO TO 670-READ
           ELSE
             MOVE SPACES          TO  WS-X (SCREEN-INDEX)
             MOVE VALID-CODE-KEY  TO  SAVE-KEY
             MOVE SAVE-CODE       TO  WS-CODE (SCREEN-INDEX)
             MOVE VALID-CODE-DESC TO  WS-DESC (SCREEN-INDEX)
             ADD      1           TO  SCREEN-INDEX.

       670-READ.
           PERFORM 30-READ-FORWARD THRU 30-EXIT
           IF EOF-SW = "Y"   OR
               VALID-CODE-TYPE NOT = SAVE-TYPE
             SUBTRACT 1 FROM SCREEN-INDEX
             MOVE SCREEN-INDEX  TO ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN
             MOVE      "Y"      TO FULL-SCREEN-SW,
                                   EOF-SW.

           IF SCREEN-INDEX > 28
             IF EOF-SW NOT = "Y"
               MOVE 28  TO ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN
               MOVE "Y" TO FULL-SCREEN-SW
               IF VALID-CODE-DESC = SPACES
                 PERFORM 671-SKIP-EMPTY-RECS THRU 671-EXIT.

       670-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       671-SKIP-EMPTY-RECS.
      *****  This paragraph is used to point to the next record in
      *****  the database that does not have a description equal
      *****  to spaces.

           PERFORM 30-READ-FORWARD THRU 30-EXIT  UNTIL
               (VALID-CODE-DESC NOT = SPACES) OR
               (EOF-SW = "Y").

           IF EOF-SW = "Y"
             MOVE 28 TO ENTRIES-ON-SCREEN.

       671-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       98-SCREEN-READ.
           READ DISPLAY-FILE FORMAT IS CGENHELP-VIEW-CFNAME
               INDICATORS ARE INDICS.
           ACCEPT IOFEEDBACK FROM I-O-FEEDBACK-AREA.
           MOVE ALL B"0" TO INDICS.
           IF DSPLY-STATUS NOT = "00"
             MOVE 3 TO VIEW-LASTKEY
           ELSE
             MOVE FUNCTION-NUM TO VIEW-LASTKEY.

       98-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       98A-SCREEN-READ.
           READ DISPLAY-FILE TERMINAL IS TERMINAL-ID
               INDICATORS ARE INDICS
                   NO DATA MOVE DSPLY-STATUS TO DSPLY-STATUS.

       98A-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       99-SCREEN-WRITE.
           WRITE DSPLY-REC FORMAT IS CGENHELP-VIEW-CFNAME
               INDICATORS ARE INDICS.

       99-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       99-BLOWUP.
           MOVE "** CGENHELP **" TO BU-DISPLAY-FLD (4).
           MOVE CGENHELP-TYPE    TO BU-DISPLAY-FLD (5).
           PERFORM 2-END-OF-JOB THRU 2-EXIT.
           GOBACK.

       99-BLOWUP-EXIT.
           EXIT.
